== sources: getting electrons in, and what gas does to them (figure 2) ==
  265 nm: 1.33e+15 photons per second per milliwatt; magnesium as installed gives 4.27 nA per milliwatt
  1e7 electrons in one turn of the 277 mm, 50 eV ring: lap 66 ns, 24.3 uA; 5684 mW of 265 nm light on magnesium as installed, 56.8 mW cleaned
  1e7 electrons in one turn of the 932 mm, 50 eV ring: lap 222 ns, 7.2 uA; 1686 mW of 265 nm light on magnesium as installed, 16.9 mW cleaned
  1e7 electrons in one turn of the 932 mm, 1 eV ring: lap 1572 ns, 1.0 uA; 238 mW of 265 nm light on magnesium as installed, 2.4 mW cleaned
  resistive cooling at D = 1 mm: 0.16 to 1.42 ms in a segment (25 to 225 kOhm), 7.35 to 22.0 ms round a lap
  a collision in exact Mathieu motion, the velocity redirected isotropically: c = 2 <dE>/E 2.025, 2.247, 2.879 at q = 0.1, 0.3, 0.5 from rest along the guide (e-fold every 1.43, 1.33, 1.12 collisions); in the steady state 1.658, 1.881, 2.513, the energy 81.8, 82.8, 85.2 % transverse (e-fold every 1.66, 1.51, 1.23 collisions)
  1e-05 mbar: 0.1 eV to the 1 eV rim in 0.331 to 0.422 ms
  1e-07 mbar: 0.1 eV to the 1 eV rim in 33.1 to 42.2 ms
  1e-09 mbar: 0.1 eV to the 1 eV rim in 3.31e+03 to 4.22e+03 ms
  at 0.1 eV resistive cooling overtakes the heating below 2.2e-06 to 2.0e-05 mbar
  at 1 eV resistive cooling overtakes the heating below 6.9e-07 to 6.2e-06 mbar
  [sources: 0.0 s]

== phase: the h = 4 ramp's longitudinal phase space, and the h = 13 ramp's numbers (figure 3) ==
  h = 4: chirp 18.0 -> 34.6 MHz in 20.5 us (135 laps), 0.811 MHz per us (h dW e / m L^2 = 0.810); 48.6 % captured at 2.73 eV rms; bucket +-3.30 eV at 50 eV, +-6.35 eV at 185 eV; Q_s 0.105 and 0.055, f_s 0.472 MHz at every energy; the spread of the 1943 captured grows 1.48 times from 58.0 to 175.0 eV, against sqrt of the energies' ratio 1.74; from lap 30 on it grows as W^0.503; the captured electrons' first synchrotron periods run 10.73 to 12.73 laps (quartiles), against 1/Q_s = 9.52 at 50 eV
  h = 13: chirp 58.5 -> 112.5 MHz in 20.5 us (135 laps), 2.635 MHz per us (h dW e / m L^2 = 2.631); 45.4 % captured at 1.58 eV rms; bucket +-1.83 eV at 50 eV, +-3.52 eV at 185 eV; Q_s 0.189 and 0.098, f_s 0.852 MHz at every energy; the spread of the 1814 captured grows 1.65 times from 58.0 to 175.0 eV, against sqrt of the energies' ratio 1.74; from lap 30 on it grows as W^0.498; the captured electrons' first synchrotron periods run 5.74 to 6.74 laps (quartiles), against 1/Q_s = 5.28 at 50 eV
  the ramp's 125.8 m of path against a free path of 40.5 m at 1e-5 mbar (sigma 1e-19 m^2, 293 K): unscattered 4.5 % at 1e-05 mbar, 73.3 % at 1e-06 mbar, 96.9 % at 1e-07 mbar
  [phase: 0.2 s]

