== resonances: a board orotron, Smith-Purcell lines, and the tune along the ramp (figure 5) ==
  Madey: -d/dpsi sinc^2(psi/2) peaks at psi = 2.606; times pi/2, 0.4242; 4 G = 1.697
  start currents at 100 eV over 1 mm: N 50, h/d 0.25, 10 kOhm: 1.1 × 10⁻⁶ A; N 50, h/d 0.25, 1 kOhm: 1.1 × 10⁻⁵ A; N 50, h/d 0.5, 1 kOhm: 2.5 × 10⁻⁴ A; N 20, h/d 0.5, 1 kOhm: 0.0039 A; 1e7 electrons round 932 mm at 100 eV carry 10.2 uA
  the 0.4-6 GHz band at normal emission: d 0.5 mm: 0.114 to 25.6 eV; d 1 mm: 0.455 to 102 eV; d 3 mm: 4.09 to 924 eV; d 10 mm: 45.5 to 1.06e+04 eV; 100 eV over 1 mm at 5.93 GHz
  1 GHz guide, 106 MHz secular: over the 135 laps of the ramp nu 23.6 -> 12.3 (50 -> 185 eV), 23 half-integer resonances crossed; d(2 nu)/dlap -0.46 -> -0.07, near a whole number at laps []...[]; mean action after the ramp with one 1 mm joint at 10 % 1.02 (over the last 12 laps 1.01 to 1.02), at 5 % 1.012 times
  5.75 GHz facing boards, 610 MHz: over the 135 laps of the ramp nu 135.6 -> 70.5 (50 -> 185 eV), 131 half-integer resonances crossed; d(2 nu)/dlap -2.67 -> -0.39, near a whole number at laps [10, 11, 44]...[48, 49, 50]; mean action after the ramp with one 1 mm joint at 10 % 1.75 (over the last 12 laps 1.75 to 2.30), at 5 % 1.040 times
  [resonances: 0.0 s]

== world: stray fields, argon's Ramsauer-Townsend window, Sagnac and Aharonov-Bohm (figure 6) ==
  a stray field E moves a held electron by eE/(m w_sec^2): 0.396 um per V/m at 106 MHz, 0.012 um per V/m at 610 MHz; the Earth's 50 uT moves a beam by evB/(m w_sec^2): 4.8 um for 185 eV, 610 MHz, 12 um for 1 eV, 106 MHz
  argon by MERT, A = -1.65 a0, alpha = 11.08 a0^3, fitted D = 47.37 a0^3 and A_1 = -12.48 a0^3 (residual 1e-12): sigma 1.1e-21 m^2 at 0.285 eV; in 1e-5 mbar an electron lives 1.72 ms at 0.1 eV, 10.5 ms at 0.25 eV, 11.6 ms at 0.285 eV, 0.461 ms at 1 eV, longest at 0.279 eV; at 10 eV with the section's 2e-19 m^2, 11 us
  Sagnac at 40.7 N: 0.822 rad per m^2; 0.0568 rad round the 932 mm circle (691 cm^2), 0.0206 rad for the trefoil's projected 251 cm^2; Aharonov-Bohm: one radian per 9.52 fT through the circle; hbar w_sec at 106 MHz 0.44 ueV (5.09 mK), 2.3e+05 quanta in 0.1 eV
  [world: 0.0 s]

